248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The upright designed for the upcoming race season is in the final stages of simulation and validation, making it one of our most refined components. The process began with a concept sketch focusing on suspension geometry and packaging constraints. After determining the load cases, we created a base CAD model and conducted finite element analysis \(FEA\). Topology optimization guided our decisions on material removal, keeping deformation within our 0.4 mm target.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Each design iteration was backed by simulation data, followed by clearance checks within the full suspension assembly. The part is designed to be machined from 7075-T6 aluminum, selected for its 503 MPa yield strength and ability to handle high loads while minimizing weight.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This year, we concentrated on streamlining the workflow and improving on past successes. The final result is an upright that maintains our desired strength and reliability while advancing simulation-driven optimization and design intent.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
